# Spring REST API

## Route prefix

```java
@RequestMapping(ApiConstants.API_V1_PREFIX + "/platforms")  // plural noun
```

## Resource paths

- Paths are resource-based nouns: `/platforms`, `/platforms/{id}`, `/platforms/{id}/payloads`
- Never use verbs in paths: no `/create`, `/update`, `/delete`, `/get`, `/edit`
- Use the HTTP verb to express intent:
  - `@GetMapping` — read
  - `@PostMapping` — create (or non-idempotent action)
  - `@PutMapping` — full update / replace
  - `@PatchMapping` — partial update
  - `@DeleteMapping` — delete

## Controller annotations

```java
@RestController
@Tag(name = "Platforms")
@SecurityRequirement(name = OpenApiConfig.X_AUTH_TOKEN)
```

## Endpoint annotations

Every endpoint needs `@Operation` with stable `operationId` (camelCase verb+resource) and `summary`:

```java
@GetMapping("/{platformId}")
@Operation(operationId = "getPlatformsPlatformId", summary = "Get platform")
```

## Response shapes

- List endpoints: return `*CollectionResponse` wrapper with `items` field — not bare `List<T>`
- Prefer DTOs over entities in controller return types
- Direct entity return is acceptable only with `// TODO: Return DTO` comment

## Command vs query controllers

- Separate `*CommandController` (mutations) from `*Controller` (reads) when domain has both
